{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>During the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> iTest, you will be introduced to Joe and Kathryn, two high school seniors. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of distinct permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b3206a02d8e690257ce3f6bb37c73792c8683bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of distinct permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15a670d2cddd15a1cc8f00ce3890f4f49faa8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KATHRYN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6df1da966cb2acec92bebecb73d3e54d1bdf3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K -J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of arrangements of the letters in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b3206a02d8e690257ce3f6bb37c73792c8683bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and the number of arrangements of the letters in KATHRYN is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86b7469f0e34e20c54cfa53de95968977fd961e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7!=5040$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />. Plugging these in, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4899488f37a67cb80f5670be9b82de7496c010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K-J=5040-6=\\boxed{5034}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"216\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td